-- title:
--   Poincaré bundle at a T'-point as a divisor difference
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, an integer $M\ge 5$ with $p\nmid M$, a characteristic-zero field $L$ that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ for $\{p\}$ together with a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta\in L$, and the intermediate field $K$ of $L\subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_1(Mp)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$, and let $j\in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81). Write $X=$ [`ModularCurve.TwoChartModel A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L229) with structure morphism $f=$ [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) to $\operatorname{Spec} A$, assumed proper. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed $A$-algebra field of characteristic $p$, let $c_1:C_1\to\operatorname{Spec} k$ and $c_2:C_2\to\operatorname{Spec} k$ be proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral, and let $i_1,i_2$ be closed immersions of $C_1,C_2$ into the base change $X\times_A k$ over $k$, whose images together cover every point of $X\times_A k$, with $\mathrm{pullback}\,i_1\,i_2$ reduced and with $n>0$ points, $n$ being given by the hypothesis `hn`. Let $\varepsilon$ be a section of $f$ over $\operatorname{Spec} A$, let $D$ be a relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ designation for $f$ (a scheme with structure morphism $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and a zero section), and assume the type of data representing the sub-Picard condition `algEquivZeroCut` — rigidified line bundles on $X\times_A T$ that are fibrewise algebraically equivalent to zero — by $D$ is nonempty; let $\mathcal{P}$ denote the Poincaré bundle of a chosen such representation. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with a ring map $\rho_O:A\to O$ carrying the maximal ideal of $A$ onto that of $O$, and a surjection $\mathrm{to}\kappa:O\to k$ with $\mathrm{to}\kappa\circ\rho_O$ the structure map $A\to k$; let $bc:X\times_A k\to X\times_A O$ be compatible with both projections via `hbc₁`, `hbc₂`. Let $T'$ be a fraction field of $O$ and $y$ a $T'$-point of $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ over $\operatorname{Spec} T'\to\operatorname{Spec} A$. Then there are $r\in\mathbb{N}$ and relative effective Cartier divisors $\bar E_1,\bar E_2$ for $f$ of fibre rank $r$ over $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\rho_O$ (ideal sheaf data on $X\times_A O$ whose closed subscheme is finite, flat and locally of finite presentation over $\operatorname{Spec} O$ of constant rank $r$) such that, for each $\nu$, the ideal $\bar E_\nu.I$ is invertible, that is, locally generated by a single non-zerodivisor, and remains so after pullback along $bc$, along $i_1$ followed by $bc$, and along $i_2$ followed by $bc$; the closed subscheme cut out by $(\bar E_\nu.I).\mathrm{comap}\,bc$ is finite over $\operatorname{Spec} k$; and the pullback of $\bar E_1.\mathrm{lineBundle}\otimes\bar E_2.\mathrm{idealModule}$, the dual of the ideal module of $\bar E_1$ tensored with the ideal module of $\bar E_2$, along the base change of $X\times_A O$ to $T'$ is isomorphic to the line bundle underlying the pullback of $\mathcal{P}$ along $y$.
--
--   This is the existence of a presentation of the Poincaré line bundle at a $T'$-valued point of the representing object for the degree-zero relative Picard functor of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ as a difference $\mathcal{O}(\bar E_1)\otimes\mathcal{O}(-\bar E_2)$ of two relative effective Cartier divisors of equal degree, spread out over the unramified discrete valuation ring $O$ and well behaved along the closed fibre and its two components. It feeds the statement on rigidified line bundles fibrewise algebraically equivalent to zero whose pullback along a point is a tensor power of the Poincaré bundle, in the analysis of the reduction of the Jacobian of $X_1(Mp)$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_exists_relEffCartierDiv_pair_isInvertible_and_pullback_lineBundle_tensor_idealModule_iso_poincare_of_map_maximalIdeal_eq_twoChartModel_x1_mul.lean

